# The upper bound of a ball with a 2-limb center, as a number of T (milestone2.md, "One
# enclosure interface", the row of lower_as and upper_as, and "The empty set and the whole line"):
# the center rounded up to T by to_up_2, then the radius added, rounded up. A bound on
# its side of every member: the whole line gives +inf, the empty ball -inf. For a finite ball
# it is less than one gap of T at c plus one gap at the result away from c + r; no number of
# steps from the directed rounding of c + r bounds it, since c + r can be far smaller than c in
# magnitude. What is claimed of the distance is the error entry: at most 5 u (|c| + r) + 3 eta,
# from the two gaps, each at most max(2 u |t|, eta), and |t| <= |c| + r + 2 u |c| + eta for the
# number t that the second rounding rounds.
kernel:        ball_upper_as_2
input:         c = c0 c1
input:         stored r
output:        h
value:         c+r
requires:      ball c r
ensures:       set_bound h above x x=c,r
ensures:       error h A c=5 k=1 t=3
min_precision: 2
source:        the center rounded up, plus the radius, rounded up (Milestone 2 listing)
license:       algorithm and proof: MIT
status:        proved
domain:        extended
ieee_status:   proved
ieee_theorem:  proofs/theories/IeeeBallConvert.v ball_upper_as_2_correct
entry:         yes
ieee_only:     yes
cone_exempt:   h is selected after the test of the radius that tells the empty ball; set_bound states what comes out for each state of the ball

a  = to_up_2(c0, c1)
t  = add_up_1(a, r)
ne = eq(r, r)
mi = neg(const inf)
h  = select(ne, t, mi)
